IraLens is a unified Internet-access system. It incorporates code and
components from two permissively licensed open-source projects, which are
implementation details of this system and are not exposed as separate
runtime identities. Neither project endorses this derivative system.

=========================================================================
1. Agent Reach — adapted source code (MIT License)
=========================================================================

Portions of this software are adapted from Agent Reach
(https://github.com/Panniantong/Agent-Reach), specifically the URL/SSRF
hardening and credential-scrubbing helpers (iralens/security.py), the
command-probing and subprocess helpers (iralens/proc.py), the private
configuration mechanism (iralens/config.py), the reader-based web
fetching with anti-bot detection (iralens/sources/web.py), and
per-platform access semantics in iralens/sources/.

